  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Instructions**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the user\'s prompt and the provided assets: nine images and eight HTML blocks. The user wants an app built with screens resembling these provided examples. I\'ll need to determine how best to leverage the HTML blocks and hotlink the images.\n\n\n**Reviewing Item Listing Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the HTML block for the \"\345\217\221\345\270\203\351\241\265 (Publish Idle Item Page)\". I\'ve noted the structure, key fields like title, condition, category, and price, along with the UI elements for photos, description, and delivery mode. I am focused on how the user interface is structured. I am thinking of how these elements work together and are presented to the user.\n\n\n**Implementing Item Interaction**\n\nI\'ve completed integrating the functionality for responding to wanted requests and submitting (which adds a new item to the home feed and user\'s items!). I\'m working with the new \"Respond to Wanted Request Page\" and integrating the logic for buyer wanted cards, item selection, and negotiation. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the interaction flow, enabling the user to select an existing item or add a new one, set a price, and arrange for a campus meetup.\n\n\n**Defining Meetup Details**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics of the meetup interaction. I have noted locations like \"\346\236\266\347\251\272\345\261\202,\" \"\344\270\200\351\243\237\345\240\202\350\245\277\351\227\250\345\217\243,\" and \"\345\233\276\346\226\207\344\277\241\346\201\257\344\270\255\345\277\203\345\244\247\345\240\202,\" and different time options. I am also working with the content for a \"\347\273\231\345\257\271\346\226\271\347\225\231\350\250\200\" section. Plus, I need to implement quick phrase buttons and the main call to action of the chat feature.\n\n\n**Constructing Interaction Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the components of the \"\346\266\210\346\201\257 (Messages List Page).\" I\'m working on the header with its badge and settings. I\'m focusing on the filter capsules, specifically those for \"\345\205\250\351\203\250\346\266\210\346\201\257,\" \"\351\235\242\344\272\244\345\276\205\347\272\246,\" and \"\347\263\273\347\273\237\351\200\232\347\237\245.\" I am incorporating the \"\344\273\212\346\227\245\351\235\242\344\272\244\347\272\246\345\256\232\" card with the meetup details, and I am also adding the conversation cards, including user details, unread indicators, timestamps, and product thumbnails.\n\n\n**Integrating Chat Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating the chat functionality. I\'m focusing on how the conversation cards function within the \"\346\266\210\346\201\257 (Messages List Page).\" I\'m implementing the detailed conversation structure. I need to make the tags work like they should. Specifically, I\'m working with the logic for opening the chat screen when a user clicks on a message. The data points from the messages are now informing the page updates.\n\n\n**Detailing Item Presentation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the presentation of individual item listings. I\'ve begun to translate the visual elements into a structured display. Key components include the aspect ratio product image, price and tag information, the item title, the seller bar including ratings and location. I also have the key bullet points, and the security banner. I am considering the flow and look for the item details page.\n\n\n**Designing Wanted Listings**\n\nI\'m now integrating the structure of the \"\346\261\202\350\264\255 (Wanted)\" section. I\'ve designed the search bar and category pills to enable easy navigation. I have implemented the \"Trust Strip\", which emphasizes the trusted nature of the transactions. I\'m focusing on the format and flow of the \"Wanted Cards,\" incorporating user details, time stamps, and the budget. The main focus is to enable easy matching between a poster and a responder.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Chat Interactions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the detailed chat interaction screen, \"\351\227\262\347\275\256\346\262\237\351\200\232 (Chat / Conversation Detail Page).\" I\'m implementing the header with the user details and actions. I\'m focusing on the pinned item card, the chat stream, with timestamps, seller and buyer messages, and the special card regarding the meetup. I\'m building out the sticky interactive bottom area with quick replies and ensuring it all looks and feels right.\n\n\n**Refining Campus Feed**\n\nI\'m now integrating the components of the home feed page (\"\351\246\226\351\241\265\"). I\'ve started on the layout, with the \"\346\270\205\350\277\234\346\240\241\345\214\272\" and student verification badges. I\'ve designed the functional zones and the search bar. I have the category tabs for the feed implemented. I am working on the quick action utilities drawer. I am currently working on the quick reply pills.\n\n\n\n**Constructing Listing Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the list components for the home feed, specifically focusing on how individual item cards are displayed. I\'m incorporating various data points, like the title, price, location and timestamp from the item details. I\'m focusing on the format and aesthetics, which includes the item image, the delivery location, and the other details to make each item appealing. I have a good grasp of the presentation for the item cards.\n\n\n**Developing Feed Items**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data and format from the provided list into the home feed. I\'m focusing on crafting individual item cards that accurately reflect each product, including their name, condition, price, and location. I am taking into account the tip card and the footer. I\'m making sure it all fits together, including the floating \"+\" button to add items.\n\n\n**Defining User Journeys**\n\nI\'m now outlining key user journeys for verification. I have two specific scenarios. The first involves browsing the home feed, navigating to a detail page, and initiating chat interactions. The second journey simulates interacting with a wanted listing, opening a response page, and making selections. My main focus is crafting the verification steps.\n\n\n**Verifying User Interactions**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on verifying the core user flows: item posting, wanted response, and user registration. I have broken the end-to-end verification into multiple steps. I am now working on clicking `\"+ \345\217\221\345\270\203\351\227\262\347\275\256\"`, which should take me to the `\345\217\221\345\270\203\351\241\265` form. Then I will submit to publish, to verify that a new item appears on both the Home Feed and My Profile. Next I will open \"\346\263\250\345\206\214\346\226\260\350\264\246\345\217\267\" from \"\346\210\221\347\232\204\" and verify registration.\n\n\n**Adapting to Desktop**\n\nI\'m now integrating desktop-specific features. I\'m focusing on the screen switcher bar for wider desktops, or ensuring all screens are accessible through in-app navigation, plus a companion preview switcher. I\'m making sure both mobile (390x844) and desktop (1440x900) viewports are clean and visually appealing with 1-click access to all 9 screens. I\'m focusing on the desktop layout, either centered or alongside a campus overview panel.\n\n\n"
