  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Modular Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the modular architecture to align with \"ultra-mode\" requirements. Specifically, I\'m focusing on `src/data/marketplaceData.ts` to house all initial data (products, requests, conversations, user profiles) alongside pure logic functions. This includes `filterProducts` and other data manipulation functions. My goal is to ensure this module is a central, pure data source.\n\n\n**Refining Core Logic Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation of core functions within `src/data/marketplaceData.ts`. This involves creating and testing functions such as `WantedItems`, `validatePublishForm`, `validateRegisterForm`, `evaluateOfferPrice`, and `filterMessages`. I\'m using `node:test` and `node:assert/strict` in `src/data/marketplaceData.test.ts` to ensure each pure logic function is robust. Concurrently, I\'ve designed the `BottomNavBar` and `HomeView`, including a functional \"FreshmanZoneView\". The goal is to establish a solid foundation of data and UI interactions.\n\n\n**Developing UI Details**\n\nI\'m presently focusing on the UI components. Specifically, I\'m working on the `WantedPlazaView`, which includes features like a campus toggle, search bar, category chips, and the `\346\210\221\346\234\211\351\227\262\347\275\256` button on wanted request cards, along with the floating `\345\217\221\346\261\202\350\264\255` button. I\'m also developing the `RespondWantedView`, concentrating on the buyer request card and its associated item selector, price offers, and location/time chips. Lastly, I\'m integrating the `PublishItemView`, ensuring features like photo thumbnails, title, condition pills, and category picker are available for item listings.\n\n\n**Implementing Chat Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the chat detail view within `src/components/ChatDetailView.tsx`. This includes the pinned item card and the message stream. I\'m focusing on the integration of the meetup confirmation card. It is linked to quick reply pills and a robust input bar. Concurrently, the unread count in the filter capsules within the MessagesView is being implemented. I\'m also planning the `0\345\205\203\351\200\201` toggle, the `\345\217\221\345\270\203\345\210\260\345\273\272\351\231\242\345\271\277\345\234\272` button, and the related campus delivery modes. I\'m trying to align with the message view\'s layout and functionalities.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1096226"
      name: "write_to_file"
