  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Critique and Fixing**\n\nI\'ve confirmed `r1-mobile-freshman.png` is an exact match to the reference image. I am now focusing on the Round 1 critique, specifically the high-severity defect related to the bottom bars. I will be looking to resolve these issues.\n\n\n**Analyzing Alignment Discrepancies**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the alignment issue for wide desktop viewports. The root cause is the left sidebar on larger screens shifting the mobile container, which breaks the intended centering of the UI elements. I am considering several fixes: wrapping the mobile container in a centered layout, using `sticky bottom-0`, or re-evaluating the screen-switcher placement to maintain alignment across all viewports.\n\n\n**Addressing Accessibility and Deep-Linking**\n\nI\'m now focusing on accessibility within `HomeView` and `FreshmanZoneView`. The current implementation using `<article onClick={...}>` is problematic, as it doesn\'t convey an interactive button role. I plan to convert the product cards to semantic `<button>` elements to ensure clear accessible names and improve keyboard navigation. I\'m also considering integrating URL query parameters for deep linking, allowing for direct navigation to specific screens like detail or messages upon initial load. This enhancement will significantly improve the application\'s testability and usability.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_185422"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Support ?screen= query parameter and keep mobile container dead-center on desktop viewports so fixed bottom bars align 100% with the mobile frame\",\"EndLine\":52,\"Instruction\":\"Initialize screen state from URL search params in src/App.tsx\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"export default function App() {\\n  const [screen, setScreen] = useState<ScreenId>(() => {\\n    const param = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get(\'screen\');\\n    const validIds: ScreenId[] = [\\n      \'home\',\\n      \'wanted\',\\n      \'publish\',\\n      \'messages\',\\n      \'profile\',\\n      \'detail\',\\n      \'freshman\',\\n      \'respond\',\\n      \'chat\',\\n      \'register\',\\n    ];\\n    if (param && validIds.includes(param as ScreenId)) {\\n      return param as ScreenId;\\n    }\\n    return \'home\';\\n  });\\n  const [historyStack, setHistoryStack] = useState<ScreenId[]>([\'home\']);\",\"StartLine\":42,\"TargetContent\":\"export default function App() {\\n  const [screen, setScreen] = useState<ScreenId>(\'home\');\\n  const [historyStack, setHistoryStack] = useState<ScreenId[]>([\'home\']);\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/App.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Adding URL query parameter support in App.tsx\",\"toolSummary\":\"Add URL screen param in App.tsx\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "replace_file_content"
    }
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_185501"
      name: "replace_file_content"
