  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Discrepancies**\n\nI\'ve been examining the visual state before and after the chat drawer opens, focusing on the user\'s comment about the selected item\'s highlight. Specifically, I\'m digging into why the user perceives a mismatch in the highlight appearance, as highlighted by the `r4-chat-drawer-open.png` screenshot. I am particularly focusing on the initial state of the UI versus the drawer open state.\n\n\n**Investigating UI Mismatch**\n\nI\'ve just reviewed the HTML 7 code, specifically focusing on the `+` button transformation when the drawer opens. My main concern is the visual mismatch created by the added border and rotation of the icon. I\'m thinking the existing circle in the `add_circle` glyph negates the need for an external border when active, potentially creating visual conflict. I will need to consider whether removing the border, or replacing it, solves the perceived mismatch as highlighted by the expert user.\n\n\n**Clarifying Visual States**\n\nI\'m now comparing the visual states of the drawer icons. I\'ve realized the initial highlight on \"\347\272\246\345\256\232\351\235\242\344\272\244\" (Meetup) is due to `selectedUtility` being pre-set to `\'meetup\'`. This causes a mismatch with the unselected, flat backgrounds of other icons in the drawer. The original HTML7 design had a soft, borderless peach, which I will compare to the highlighted versions, as well as the unselected versions of the other icons, to improve consistency. The expert\'s feedback will be invaluable.\n\n\n**Refining Icon Highlights**\n\nI\'m now focused on the active highlight state of the drawer items. My goal is to ensure consistency, specifically for the active highlight\'s visual appearance. I want to match the `bg-primary-fixed text-primary` token used in the design system to any item that is `activeToolModal`. Also, I\'m examining the `input` bar, in particular its HTML7 representation. I\'ve noted the absence of a ring and double-circle border for the microphone and add_circle icons, which I want to bring to parity.\n\n\n**Evaluating Visual Consistency**\n\nI\'m now examining the visual consistency between the input bar and the quick action utility drawer. I see the input bar\'s `mic` and `add_circle` buttons lack the outer ring and double-circle border. This contrasts with the utility items\' highlighted states, which use a `rounded-xl bg-primary` style. I want to align the UI by either applying the ring to both areas or removing it entirely.\n\n\n"
