    thinking: "**Analyzing the Selector**\n\nOkay, I\'m now digging into the provided CSS selector. My focus is on understanding the targeting strategy used. I\'m breaking down each component to figure out how it identifies a specific element within the HTML structure. Currently, I\'m working my way through the chain of selectors to grasp its hierarchical precision.\n\n\n**Tracing the Element\'s Location**\n\nI\'ve successfully traced the target element within the `HomeView.tsx` structure. It\'s the `div` containing the four campus zone buttons, each with its associated label. The user\'s request is clear: implement similar secondary pages for the other buttons like the existing `FreshmanZoneView`. Now checking that secondary page to implement.\n\n\n**Examining the Page\'s Structure**\n\nI\'m now closely examining the layout and styling details of the zone\'s page, specifically its primary components. I\'ve broken down the TopAppBar, noting the sticky bar\'s elements: back button, zone title, and search toggle. I\'ve also identified the sub-category filter bar with its active and inactive pills. The two-column product grid with square cards follows the design of each component.\n\n\n**Dissecting the Component Details**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on dissecting the component details of a typical product card and campus tip box, to mimic and integrate these elements. I\'m focusing on the product card\'s structure, including the image (with scaling on hover), badge (e.g., \"9\346\210\220\346\226\260\"), title, price, and pickup location, as well as the campus tip box\'s layout, icon, and text. I\'m noting each class name for design replication.\n\n\n**Defining the Freshman Zone**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the contents of the \'freshman\' zone. I\'m noting the title, sub-tabs, and specific items to be displayed on this page. My goal is to structure this zone to match the specifications. I need to ensure a consistent look and feel with the existing pages while tailoring it to this specific zone\'s content.\n\n\n**Constructing the Graduation Zone**\n\nI\'m now focused on constructing the Graduation Zone. I\'ve outlined its title and defined the sub-tabs: \'\345\205\250\351\203\250\', \'\346\225\260\347\240\201\347\224\265\345\231\250\', \'\345\257\235\345\256\244\345\270\246\350\265\260\', \'\344\273\243\346\255\245\345\267\245\345\205\267\', and \'\346\211\223\345\214\205\347\211\271\346\203\240\'. I\'m compiling the six specific items. I\'m leveraging `HOTLINK_IMAGES` to integrate the product images. Each item includes details such as condition, price, pickup location, and sub-category. I\'m aiming for accurate data representation.\n\n\n**Defining the Textbooks Zone**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the textbook zone. I\'ve set the title and sub-tabs: \'\345\205\250\351\203\250\', \'\345\273\272\347\255\221\345\267\245\347\250\213\', \'\345\270\202\346\224\277\346\234\272\347\224\265\', \'\350\200\203\350\257\201\344\272\214\345\273\272\', and \'\344\270\223\345\215\207\346\234\254\350\200\203\347\240\224\'. I\'ve also identified the six specific items. My immediate task is to accurately format all data points for display. I\'m focusing on ensuring data integrity with item details, sub-categories and `HOTLINK_IMAGES`.\n\n\n**Populating the Freebie Zone**\n\nI\'m currently populating the \'\345\205\215\350\264\271\344\272\222\345\212\251\' (Freebie) zone, defining its structure and content. I\'ve set up the title and defined the sub-tabs: \'\345\205\250\351\203\250\', \'\350\200\203\350\257\201\347\254\224\350\256\260\', \'\345\256\277\350\210\215\346\227\245\347\224\250\', \'\351\227\262\347\275\256\346\225\260\347\240\201\', and \'\347\273\277\346\244\215\346\226\207\345\205\267\'.  I\'m focusing on accurately capturing the details for each of the six free items, including condition, pickup location, and sub-category.\n\n\n"
