cation via `playwright-cli` within the `run_command`. The plan involves launching `http://localhost:3000`, resizing the viewport to 1440x900, capturing a desktop screenshot at `.playwright-cli/r1-desktop.png`, and checking the console. This should set a baseline for this test round.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT\\\\nmkdir -p .playwright-cli && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  playwright-cli open --browser=chromium http://localhost:3000 && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  playwright-cli resize 1440 900 && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  playwright-cli screenshot --filename=.playwright-cli/r1-desktop.png && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\n<truncated 186 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Capturing desktop and mobile screenshots and DOM snapshot\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Capture initial screenshots and snapshot\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":40,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T08:59:58Z\",\"input_tokens\":2119,\"cache_read_tokens\":190623,\"output_tokens\":163,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/.playwright-cli/r1-desktop.png\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing desktop screenshot r1-desktop.png\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View r1-desktop.png\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/.playwright-cli/r1-mobile-home.png\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing mobile home screenshot r1-mobile-home.png\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View r1-mobile-home.png\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":43,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:00:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":2526,\"cache_read_tokens\":192743,\"output_tokens\":609,\"thinking\":\"**Observing Desktop Layout**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining `r1-desktop.png` closely. My focus is the desktop layout, specifically at 1440x900. I\'ve pinpointed a crucial observation: the `BottomNavBar`, along with the fixed bottom docks in views like `PublishItemView`, `ItemDetailView`, and others, presents a certain configuration.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT\\\\nplaywright-cli open --browser=chromium http://localhost:3000 && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  playwright-cli resize 390 844 && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  playwright-cli click e94 && \\\\\\\\\\\\n  playwright-cli screenshot --filename=.playwright-cli/r1-mobile-freshman.png &&\\n<truncated 455 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Capturing mobile screenshots of freshman, detail, wanted, and publish screens\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Capture 4 mobile screens\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":45,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:00:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":3285,\"cache_read_tokens\":193220,\"output_tokens\":197,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Accessibility Failures**\\n\\nI\'ve started by examining the screenshot of the mobile view and pinpointing why the \\\"article\\\" element on the HomeView lacked accessible button attributes. I\'m focusing on the accessibility implications and why it didn\'t conform. I\'m recalling section 2 of \\\"ultra-mode,\\\" which suggests using native elements.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/.playwright-cli/r1-mobile-freshman.png\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing mobile freshman zone screenshot\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View r1-mobile-freshman.png\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":47,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:00:56Z\",\"input_tokens\":3421,\"cache_read_tokens\":194456,\"output_tokens\":5366,\"thinking\":\"**Reviewing Critique and Fixing**\\n\\nI\'ve confirmed `r1-mobile-freshman.png` is an exact match to the reference image. I am now focusing on the Round 1 critique, specifically the high-severity defect related to the bottom bars. I will be looking to resolve these issues.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Alignment Discrepancies**\\n\\nI\'ve zeroed in on the alignment issue for wide desktop viewports. The root cause is the left sidebar on larger screens shifting the mobile container, which breaks the intended centering of the UI elemen\\n<truncated 332 bytes>\\n current implementation using `<article onClick={...}>` is problematic, as it doesn\'t convey an interactive button role. I plan to convert the product cards to semantic `<button>` elements to ensure clear accessible names and improve keyboard navigation. I\'m also considering integrating URL query parameters for deep linking, allowing for direct navigation to specific screens like detail or messages upon initial load. This enhancement will significantly improve the application\'s testability and usability.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Support ?screen= query parameter and keep mobile container dead-center on desktop viewports so fixed bottom bars align 100% with the mobile frame\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"52\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Initialize screen state from URL search params in src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"export default function App() {\\\\n  const [screen, setScreen] = useState<ScreenId>(() => {\\\\n    const param = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get(\'screen\');\\\\n    const validIds: ScreenId[] = [\\\\n      \'home\',\\\\n      \'wanted\',\\\\n      \'publish\',\\\\n\\n<truncated 332 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"42\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"export default function App() {\\\\n  const [screen, setScreen] = useState<ScreenId>(\'home\');\\\\n  const [historyStack, setHistoryStack] = useState<ScreenId[]>([\'home\']);\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Adding URL query parameter support in App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add URL screen param in App.tsx\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Center the mobile container on desktop and position the desktop switcher panel on the left so fixed bottom bars stay centered inside the mobile viewport\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"354\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update desktop layout in src/App.tsx so the mobile viewport is centered on screen\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  return (\\\\n    <div className=\\\\\\\"min-h-screen bg-[#F3F2F7] text-on-surface flex justify-center relative\\\\\\\">\\\\n      {/* Desktop Companion Screen Switcher (Pinned Left on Wide Viewports so Mobile Frame stays Dead-Center) */}\\\\n      <aside\\\\n        aria-label\\n<truncated 3197 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"276\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"  return (\\\\n    <div className=\\\\\\\"min-h-screen bg-[#F3F2F7] text-on-surface flex justify-center lg:py-6 lg:px-8\\\\\\\">\\\\n      <div className=\\\\\\\"w-full max-w-6xl flex items-start justify-center gap-8\\\\\\\">\\\\n        {/* Desktop Companion Screen Switcher (Hidden on M\\n<truncated 3378 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Centering mobile viewport on desktop in App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Center mobile viewport in App.tsx\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Close wrapper div in App.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"455\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Remove extra wrapper div closing tag in src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"          {screen === \'register\' && (\\\\n            <RegisterView\\\\n              onBack={goBack}\\\\n              onCompleteRegister={(selectedCp) => {\\\\n                setCampus(selectedCp);\\\\n                navigateTo(\'profile\');\\\\n              }}\\\\n       \\n<truncated 57 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"440\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"          {screen === \'register\' && (\\\\n            <Regist