  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering UI Design**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on user request number five, specifically the UI design aspects. I\'m taking the suggestion to add a secondary page and mimic the interface of the \"\346\226\260\347\224\237\344\270\223\345\214\272\" (New Student Zone). I\'m looking at applying style changes to specific elements, starting with the CSS selector provided.\n\n\n**Tracing Element Locations**\n\nI\'ve been tracing the provided CSS selector, identifying the specific HTML elements it targets within `App.tsx` and `HomeView.tsx`. The selector leads to a `div` element containing the Campus Functional Zones within `HomeView.tsx`, providing a clear understanding of the target element\'s context. I can now proceed to explore how to modify the CSS and UI.\n\n\n**Expanding Zone Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving into adding secondary pages for the remaining zones: \"\346\257\225\344\270\232\346\270\205\344\273\223\", \"\346\225\231\346\235\220\350\257\276\344\273\266\", and \"\345\205\215\350\264\271\344\272\222\345\212\251\". Currently, only \"\346\226\260\347\224\237\344\270\223\345\214\272\" has a dedicated secondary page; the rest toggle a filter. I\'m taking the user\'s advice to mimic the \"\346\226\260\347\224\237\344\270\223\345\214\272\" design for consistency. I see how to update the handleZoneClick method to add navigation, and I\'ll focus on how to render content to mirror the FreshmanZoneView\'s style in those new pages.\n\n\n"
