w detailing the component elements. The horizontal scroll container will use several Tailwind classes: `overflow-x-auto`, `no-scrollbar`, `pb-1`, `-mx-5`, `px-5`, `snap-x`, and `snap-mandatory` for edge-to-edge scrolling with card alignment to page margins. Each \"Hot Wanted Card\" will be a `w-[248px]` rectangle, shrinking and snapping to start. Inside, I\'ll structure the card with a top row for user info and time, a middle section for content, and a bottom row.\n\n\n**Refining Card Interactions**\n\nI\'m now refining the Hot Wanted Card\'s interactions and appearance. The left section now displays the budget and pickup location, using appropriate text styles. On the right, a prominent \"\346\210\221\346\234\211\351\227\262\347\275\256\" button triggers the `onRespondWanted` function, navigating directly to the `RespondWantedView`. I\'ve added a \"More / Post Wanted\" card for user interaction.\n\n\n"
